6. DATABASE SCHEMA (POSTGRESQL) & SECURITY REQUIREMENTS
====================================================================
- Core Tables: `roles`, `users`, `connected_accounts`, `account_authorizations` (AES-256-GCM encrypted tokens), `market_instruments`, `market_data_cache`, `virtual_orders`, `bot_strategies`, `cashier_transactions`, `watchlists`, `notifications`, `email_logs`, `application_settings`, `administrator_audit_logs`, `security_logs`.
- Security Rules: Never log or return raw Deriv OAuth/API tokens or secrets to frontend; enforce JWT `requireAuth` + RBAC `requireAdmin`; use parameterized SQL queries only; provide `.env.example` covering `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, `DERIV_APP_ID`, `DERIV_CLIENT_SECRET`, `DERIV_OAUTH_URL`, `DERIV_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI`, `DERIV_OAUTH_SCOPES`, `DERIV_WS_URL`, `BREVO_API_KEY`, `FRONTEND_URL`, and `ADMIN_PRIVATE_SLUG`.